    "origin_id": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/2027-dodge-charger-gets-special-edition-package-celebrating-90-years-of-mopar-277643.html",
    "canonical_url": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/2027-dodge-charger-gets-special-edition-package-celebrating-90-years-of-mopar-277643.html",
    "origin_publisher": "autoevolution",
    "published_at": "2026-10-27T17:08:15+00:00",
    "published_at_raw": "2026-10-27T17:08:15+0000",
    "publication_precision": "TIMESTAMP",
    "acquired_at": "2026-10-27T19:17:24.697248+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-10-27T19:17:24.697248+00:00",
    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • Toyota Puts Snow Tracks on Five SUVs and Trucks, Unloads Them at SEMA 2026 as the Snowhunter Bunch\n2027 Dodge Charger Gets Special-Edition Package Celebrating 90 Years of Mopar\n7 photos\nPhoto: Stellantis\nThe 2026 SEMA Show is just around the corner, and, unsurprisingly, Mopar joins the event to showcase a new special-edition package. It's called Exclusive Mopar '27, celebrates 90 years of Mopar \"passion, performance, and personalization,\" and graces two versions of the 2027 Dodge Charger.\nThe package is available on the Charger R/T and Scat Pack Plus, both two-door coupes with turbocharged inline-six powerplants. Regardless of the choice, customers will get carbon-fiber upgrades like a front splitter, a rear spoiler, and a carbon-fiber hood.\nThe lightweight hood includes a functional scoop, while the cars will have a unique graphics package. Exclusive Mopar '27 will be limited to three exterior colors, Bludicrous, Diamond Black, and White Knuckle.\nBased on the only official photo available as of this writing, the black and white cars will get blue stripes, while the blue Charger will get black stripes. The bundle will also include a limited-series plaque mounted under the hood and a unique badge on the dashboard. Speaking of which, Mopar wants to produce only 270 units.\nAnd I'm not talking about 270 examples each; that's the total for both the R/T and Scat Pack Plus. The production will be split into 90 vehicles offered in each of the three exterior colors. Exactly 243 of these cars will be sold in the United States, with the remaining 27 examples available in Canada. Production will begin in the spring of 2027. Dealer orders begin in early January 2027.\nHow much does it cost to add the Exclusive Mopar '27 bundle to a Charger? The package costs $10,995. That's a 20% premium for the Charger R/T, which comes in at $49,995 before options. All told, the R/T with the said bundle will set you back $60,990 before you start adding other options. The Scat Pack Plus model starts from $59,990, which means you'll pay a total of $70,985 to take it home with the limited-edition Mopar treatment.\nThe Mopar '27 package will make an appearance at the 2026 SEMA Show , but it will actually debut a few days earlier. Stellantis will introduce it at the Mopar NHRA Las Vegas Nationals at the Las Vegas Motor Speedway on October 30. The cars will be on display through November 1. You'll then be able to see them at the Las Vegas Convention Center between November 3 and 6.\nMopar '27 is the 15th annual package introduced around the SEMA Show since 2011. There should be 16, but the 2020 edition was cancelled due to the Covid-19 pandemic. The series began with the Charger in 2011, with the nameplate returning in 2015 and 2023. The 300, Dart, Challenger, Durango, Jeep Gladiator, and Ram also received similar treatments over the years.\nAs a brief reminder, the 2027 Dodge Charger R/T comes with a twin-turbo, 3.0-liter inline-six (SIXPACK) setup good for 420 horsepower. It hits 60 mph in 4.6 seconds and runs the quarter-mile in 12.9 clicks. The Scat Pack Plus model has larger turbochargers, standard AWD, and packs 550 horsepower. Hitting 60 mph takes only 3.9 seconds, toward a quarter-mile run of 12.2 seconds.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\ndodge charger 2027 dodge charger Mopar 2026 sema show Scat Pack muscle car\nAbout the author: Ciprian Florea\nAsk Ciprian about cars and he'll reveal an obsession with classics and an annoyance with modern design cues. Read his articles and you'll understand why his ideal SUV is the 1969 Chevrolet K5 Blazer. Full profile\nUP NEXT Triumph Reveals the 2027 Tiger 1200 as the Most Everything Adventure Bike It Ever Made",
